CloakingSpeed= (patch 0247, S). Retail: SUB/SQD/DLPH/BSUB cloak fade length + re-cloak step;
current cloak is a state flag with no fade. Per-type fade/re-cloak from CloakingSpeed=:
AnType::cloak_fade_frames (frames, 0 = instant legacy), AnUnit::cloak_left_frames countdown.
Firing snaps surfaced and pins the fade while the global CloakDelay runs; afterwards the
sub re-cloaks one step per frame. submerged flips only when fully re-cloaked; the draw
tint interpolates 255 -> 128 across the fade. Save format 70. Test in test_w7_airnav.cpp:
fade pins through CloakDelay then steps home, and a key-less type re-cloaks instantly.

